+# Shared deployed playback pilot
+
+Owns canonical routed source reconstruction, crossover evidence, post-DSP level
+recalibration and the existing WAV/sidecar resource adapters consumed by both
+routed processing and final selection. All DSP realization remains delegated to
+roomeq-engine; this owner has no dependency on a workflow or either coordinator.
+
+This is an isolated Phase 5 prototype. Existing workflow public entry points and
+all current behavioral test bodies remain in place through explicit imports.
+Private capture fields and acquisition receipts remain untouched. The new public
+helper surface, resource ownership, test placement, compiler/feature closure,
+correctness, build time and memory must be evaluated before accepting this cut.
+
+The causal-delay and electrical-path assessment modules move with every existing
+unit-test body. The original workflow module paths explicitly reexport the same
+public and crate-private items. The three existing fixture helpers are copied
+verbatim under cfg(test) solely for the moved electrical tests; no production
+algorithm is duplicated and the fixture copy has no workflow dependency.
+
+The EQ-resource and first-channel WAV adapters move with their six existing
+behavior tests. The f32 first-channel decoder and f64 multi-channel decoder
+retain their distinct contracts and are not merged. Immutable intake evidence
+and timing admission move below both consumers; application conditioning and
+its tests remain in workflow. Three tests that call the complete optimize_room
+pipeline move unchanged into the existing qa_contract integration executable.
+Final resource binding still reads only through ArtifactStore and preserves
+stage-ownership checks, resource validation, retained-tap checks, and hashes.
+
+This source overlay maps 98 preexisting cases: 95 below the shared owner and
+three in the existing QA integration target. This is a source-level map, not a
+compiler or execution proof. Further routed/finalization extraction, measured
+critical paths, full feature graphs and acceptance decisions remain open.
+
+Measurement loading, FIR target resolution, acquisition-timing validation,
+delivered decision-ledger reconciliation and target reconciliation use this
+same shared production owner. The original final-ledger child module is deleted
+from workflow when materializing the overlay, avoiding a retained orphan copy.
+All new API and dependency costs remain part of the conditional-cut evaluation.
